00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:37,181
Please try again.

259
00:33:40,810 --> 00:33:43,396
Please try again.

260
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:49,152
Thank you, General Perez.

261
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:25,396
Well?

262
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:30,068
Are you gonna kill me, or what?

263
00:34:32,695 --> 00:34:34,739
There's no point, is there?

264
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:37,075
They've taken it out of you.

265
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:40,411
Where is it? Is it on the ship?

266
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:44,415
You mean my baby?

267
00:34:46,125 --> 00:34:51,255
I don't get it. If they took it out,
why are they keeping you alive?

268
00:34:51,422 --> 00:34:55,551
Well, they're curious. I'm the latest thing.

269
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:08,272
Look, I can make it all stop.

270
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:12,443
The pain, this nightmare.
That's all I can offer you.

271
00:35:20,868 --> 00:35:25,373
What makes you think
I would let you do that?

272
00:35:29,335 --> 00:35:31,129
Who are you?

273
00:35:31,295 --> 00:35:34,757
Ripley, Ellen. Lieutenant first class.

274
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:37,927
Number 36706.

275
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:42,557
Ellen Ripley died 200 years ago.

276
00:35:43,933 --> 00:35:45,143
You're not her.

277
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:49,689
I'm not her?

278
00:35:56,279 --> 00:36:00,283
- Who am I?
- You're a thing, a construct.

279
00:36:00,450 --> 00:36:03,411
They grew you in a fucking lab.

280
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:06,539
And now they brought it out of you.

281
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:08,875
Not all the way out.

282
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:17,341
I can feel it.

283
00:36:17,508 --> 00:36:20,219
Behind my eyes.

284
00:36:20,386 --> 00:36:22,930
I can hear it moving.

285
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:29,395
You gotta help me stop this thing
before it gets loose.

286
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:35,693
It's too late.

287
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:38,446
You can't stop it.

288
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:40,698
It's inevitable.

289
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:46,454
Not as long as I'm around.

290
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:48,998
You'll never get out of here alive.

291
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:52,752
I don't care.

292
00:36:52,919 --> 00:36:54,712
Really?

293
00:36:57,215 --> 00:36:59,634
I can make it stop.

294
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:09,143
Go on, get out of here.

295
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:11,437
They're looking for you.

296
00:37:23,199 --> 00:37:28,162
I think you're gonna find that this was
very ill-advised. Where are her friends?

297
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:32,875
- They're in the mess hall, sir.
- Well, you find them now. Quietly.

298
00:37:33,251 --> 00:37:37,839
- What the hell is going on here?
- It smells like a double-cross, boss.

299
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:42,093
Where's the other one? With the chair?

300
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:45,471
Don't ever touch me. Ever!

301
00:37:46,305 --> 00:37:47,682
Wanna tell us what this is?

302
00:37:47,849 --> 00:37:49,934
- Wanna tell me who you're working for?
- What?

303
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:53,312
- Wren, they got nothing to do with this.
- To do with what?

304
00:37:53,521 --> 00:37:56,357
Do you know what the penalties
for terrorist activity are?

305
00:37:56,524 --> 00:37:59,485
No terrorists in my crew.
Call, something you wanna tell me?

306
00:37:59,652 --> 00:38:04,240
I don't care whether you knew or not. You
brought a terrorist onboard a military vessel.

307
00:38:04,407 --> 00:38:07,660
And as far as I am concerned,
you all die with her.

308
00:38:09,787 --> 00:38:11,998
Do you understand?

309
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:16,169
Yeah.

310
00:38:16,335 --> 00:38:18,296
I understand.

311
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:22,091
Christie.

312
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:31,851
Freeze!

313
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:42,403
Stop! Drop your weapons!

314
00:38:42,570 --> 00:38:46,324
And you, drop that piece of shit!
Or I blow his head off!

315
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,826
- I can't do that, man.
- Drop it now!

316
00:38:48,993 --> 00:38:51,412
- Can't, they're attached.
- I'm not fucking with you!

317
00:38:51,621 --> 00:38:54,790
You're all under arrest for a Code 8,
which is concealed weapons...

318
00:38:54,957 --> 00:38:57,835
...and a Code 12, which is murder.
Release Dr.--

319
00:38:58,002 --> 00:39:00,004
- Kiss my ass.
- Put down your weapons!

320
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:08,387
Everybody okay?

321
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:14,018
Real easy, soldier boy.

322
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:19,023
Security, there is a serious problem
in the mess hall.

323
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:21,859
You lie to me now, little girl...

324
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:26,614
...I will cut your throat and
leave you here to die. Understand?

325
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:28,491
- This is Security, Section 2.
- Hello?

326
00:39:28,658 --> 00:39:30,326
- We do not read you.
- Goddamn. Hello?

327
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:33,329
- We do not copy you. Please repeat.
- Hello?

328
00:39:33,496 --> 00:39:34,538
Please repeat.

329
00:41:08,758 --> 00:41:10,634
Gediman!

330
00:41:10,801 --> 00:41:13,512
He's conducting illegal experiments,
breeding...

331
00:41:13,679 --> 00:41:18,559
- Ice the goddamn mole.
- Listen, he is breeding an alien species.

332
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:21,771
Dangerous. If it gets loose,
it'll make the Lacerta plague...

333
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:24,982
- ...look like a fucking square dance.
- Shut up!

334
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:28,861
Listen.

335
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:33,616
Your attention, please. Security breach.

336
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:36,327
Medlab, Level 15.

337
00:42:30,631 --> 00:42:34,301
Let's get back to the <i>Betty.</i> The doctor
and soldier boy can see us to the door.

338
00:42:34,468 --> 00:42:36,595
- What about Vriess?
- Fuck Vriess.

339
00:42:47,773 --> 00:42:49,733
Your attention, please.

340
00:42:49,900 --> 00:42:53,112
Unauthorized opening of Cage 3.

341
00:42:53,279 --> 00:42:56,740
Unauthorized opening of Cages 5...

342
00:42:56,907 --> 00:43:00,327
...7, 8, 10.

343
00:43:00,494 --> 00:43:02,705
- Move it! Now!
- Evacuation.

344
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:05,791
- Go! Go! Go!
- Evacuation.

345
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:18,471
This is not a drill.

346
00:43:27,771 --> 00:43:30,149
- Evacuation.
- Get on board!

347
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:34,862
Your attention, please.
Nonhuman presence detected.

348
00:43:35,571 --> 00:43:38,699
Levels 21, 23.

349
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:41,118
Twenty-seven.

350
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:42,620
Fourteen.

351
00:43:42,786 --> 00:43:44,955
Level 38.

352
00:43:45,122 --> 00:43:47,249
Level 39.

353
00:43:49,126 --> 00:43:53,297
Evacuation. Proceed to lifeboats.

354
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,466
This is not a drill.

355
00:43:55,674 --> 00:43:58,344
Thank you for your cooperation.

356
00:45:05,035 --> 00:45:08,122
I'll give you holes, you slimy bastard!

357
00:45:13,043 --> 00:45:14,211
Move it! Go!

358
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:16,922
- Final lifeboat ready for launch.
- Get on board!

359
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:27,808
- Go!
- Complete evacuation now.

360
00:45:34,315 --> 00:45:35,983
No!

361
00:45:36,483 --> 00:45:37,651
Grenade.

362
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:33,791
Alert. Alert.

363
00:46:33,957 --> 00:46:36,126
Evacuation incomplete.

364
00:46:37,127 --> 00:46:40,798
Civilian presence detected in Area H.

365
00:46:40,964 --> 00:46:45,469
Warning,
main vessel declared uninhabitable.

366
00:46:53,102 --> 00:46:56,480
- Elgyn, come on. Let's move, man.
- Yeah.

367
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:20,731
Elgyn? Elgyn, where are you?

368
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:32,117
Elgyn, where are you?

369
00:48:34,786 --> 00:48:36,705
Elgyn!

370
00:49:14,409 --> 00:49:16,161
Elgyn!

371
00:49:16,787 --> 00:49:19,831
- Oh, my God. Elgyn!
- Elgyn?

372
00:49:19,998 --> 00:49:21,625
Elgyn?

373
00:49:22,918 --> 00:49:24,378
Elgyn?

374
00:49:25,128 --> 00:49:26,672
Easy, Hillard!

375
00:49:26,838 --> 00:49:30,050
- Give me a hand. Give me a hand here!
- Get him up! Get him up!

376
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:32,970
- Come on, let's get him up.
- Move out of the way!

377
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:34,805
Shit.

378
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:38,308
- What the fuck did this?
- What's in this place?

379
00:49:44,314 --> 00:49:46,608
- Call, get down!
- What the fuck is that?

380
00:49:46,775 --> 00:49:49,403
Don't shoot! It's in front of the hull!

381
00:49:51,989 --> 00:49:55,325
- What is that?
- Come on, man, time to go. Time to go.

382
00:49:55,492 --> 00:49:56,493
Get back!

383
00:49:59,997 --> 00:50:01,164
Time to go!

384
00:50:01,331 --> 00:50:02,708
Come on, Call!

385
00:50:03,208 --> 00:50:04,918
Open the goddamn door!

386
00:50:05,085 --> 00:50:10,090
We can't open it! We can't open that.
We can't open the door!

387
00:50:14,261 --> 00:50:18,599
- We gotta go back!
- I'm not going back. You go back.

388
00:50:43,999 --> 00:50:45,709
What the fuck?

389
00:50:48,211 --> 00:50:51,006
Was it everything you hoped for?

390
00:50:52,174 --> 00:50:54,092
Leave him alone.

391
00:51:03,310 --> 00:51:05,979
What do we do now, man?

392
00:51:06,146 --> 00:51:09,316
Same thing we're doing.
We get the hell out of here.

393
00:51:09,483 --> 00:51:11,735
What if there's more?

394
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:15,739
I say we stay here, man.
Let the army guys deal.

395
00:51:15,906 --> 00:51:20,202
- Where the fuck are the army guys?
- They're dead.

396
00:51:20,369 --> 00:51:23,246
- Then we don't need this asshole anymore.
- Step back!

397
00:51:23,413 --> 00:51:24,998
- No, you step back.
- Stop it!

398
00:51:25,165 --> 00:51:26,792
You got no authority here!

399
00:51:29,586 --> 00:51:32,464
Doctor, that thing that killed my partner.

400
00:51:32,631 --> 00:51:36,093
- That's your pet science project?
- Yes.

401
00:51:36,259 --> 00:51:39,513
- Let me do him right now, man.
- I should let him do you right now.

402
00:51:39,930 --> 00:51:42,015
How many more are there?

403
00:51:42,182 --> 00:51:44,351
How many more are there?

404
00:51:44,518 --> 00:51:45,519
Twelve.

405
00:51:48,397 --> 00:51:50,440
Twelve?

406
00:51:50,607 --> 00:51:51,942
Twelve.

407
00:51:54,277 --> 00:51:56,530
Twelve.

408
00:51:56,697 --> 00:51:58,532
There'll be more.

409
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:05,414
So who do I have to fuck
to get off this boat?

410
00:52:08,125 --> 00:52:11,586
I can get you off.
Maybe not the boat, but...

411
00:52:13,422 --> 00:52:14,631
Let's get out of here.

412
00:52:14,798 --> 00:52:18,051
No, wait a second here.
She was the host for these monsters.

413
00:52:18,218 --> 00:52:21,346
Wren cloned her
because she had one inside her.

414
00:52:21,513 --> 00:52:23,223
She's not human.

415
00:52:23,974 --> 00:52:27,310
She was part of his experiment
and she will turn on us in a second.

416
00:52:27,477 --> 00:52:30,856
- I don't give a shit what she is.
- She's too much of a risk.

417
00:52:31,022 --> 00:52:33,275
- We have to leave her.
- She comes.

418
00:52:33,817 --> 00:52:37,195
- We can't trust her.
- I don't trust anyone.

419
00:52:41,491 --> 00:52:46,163
If we're gonna survive this mess,
we all stick together. Agreed?

420
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,176
Hillard, we gotta go.

421
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:01,595
It's not over. We gotta get to the <i>Betty.</i>

422
00:53:30,582 --> 00:53:33,043
Make a nice souvenir.

423
00:53:41,176 --> 00:53:44,971
- I can't believe you did that.
- Did what?

424
00:53:45,138 --> 00:53:47,265
Killed one. It's like killing your own kind.

425
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:49,768
It was in my way.

426
00:54:13,708 --> 00:54:14,835
Oh, man.

427
00:54:18,922 --> 00:54:21,800
Who were you expecting? Santa Claus?

428
00:54:22,884 --> 00:54:25,887
I thought you were toast for certain, man.

429
00:54:26,888 --> 00:54:29,224
Where's Elgyn?

430
00:54:32,602 --> 00:54:35,313
- Shit.
- What if they're all over the <i>Betty?</i>

431
00:54:35,647 --> 00:54:38,692
All the activity's been in the F sector.
Why would they move?

432
00:54:38,859 --> 00:54:42,904
They won't.
If they send anyone out, it'll be...

433
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:44,739
...here.

434
00:54:45,282 --> 00:54:47,284
Where the meat is.

435
00:54:47,576 --> 00:54:51,580
Yeah. Well, I say if we wanna make
any decent time, I say we ditch the cripple.

436
00:54:53,665 --> 00:54:56,334
- No offense, man.
- None taken.

437
00:54:56,501 --> 00:54:58,461
Nobody is left behind.

438
00:54:59,045 --> 00:55:01,256
Not even you, Johner.

439
00:55:02,757 --> 00:55:06,970
- What's the quickest way out of here?
- After the cooling tower, there's an elevator.

440
00:55:07,137 --> 00:55:10,473
It runs from the top of the ship
down to engineering, Level 1 deck.

441
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:14,728
- Take us straight to the dock.
- Sounds reasonable. Let's do it.

442
00:55:16,146 --> 00:55:18,481
We're moving.

443
00:55:18,648 --> 00:55:22,319
- What?
- The ship is moving. I can feel it.

444
00:55:22,819 --> 00:55:26,239
The ship has stealth-run.
There's no way you can tell.

445
00:55:27,616 --> 00:55:31,119
- She's right.
- The ship's been go since the attack.

446
00:55:31,494 --> 00:55:34,164
It's a standard emergency procedure.

447
00:55:34,331 --> 00:55:38,376
That's right. Any serious problem,
the ship autopilots back to home base.

448
00:55:38,543 --> 00:55:41,171
And you were planning on
letting us know this?

449
00:55:41,338 --> 00:55:43,506
Nobody asked.

450
00:55:43,673 --> 00:55:46,009
What's home base?

451
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:50,722
Earth.

452
00:55:51,097 --> 00:55:53,224
- Great.
- Bastard.

453
00:55:53,391 --> 00:55:56,853
Earth? I'd rather stay here
with the things, man.

454
00:55:57,646 --> 00:56:00,899
- How long until we get to Earth?
- Three hours almost.

455
00:56:01,066 --> 00:56:03,109
We gotta blow the ship.

456
00:56:03,276 --> 00:56:05,987
Call! You're not blowing this ship.

457
00:56:06,821 --> 00:56:09,282
Not while we're on it, okay?

458
00:56:09,449 --> 00:56:12,661
We get out of the ship,
you do as you please, all right?

459
00:56:14,746 --> 00:56:17,832
Earth, man. What a shithole.

460
00:56:25,590 --> 00:56:27,467
It's clear.

461
00:56:33,723 --> 00:56:35,642
Hey, Ripley.

462
00:56:39,396 --> 00:56:44,025
I heard you, like,
ran into these things before.

463
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:47,529
- That's right.
- Wow, man.

464
00:56:47,696 --> 00:56:51,241
So, like, what did you do?

465
00:56:53,743 --> 00:56:55,704
I died.

466
00:57:22,397 --> 00:57:24,441
Not that way!

467
00:57:29,696 --> 00:57:31,448
Ripley.

468
00:57:37,954 --> 00:57:40,123
Ripley, come on.

469
00:57:42,667 --> 00:57:45,712
Ripley, we got no time for sightseeing here.

470
00:57:49,966 --> 00:57:52,302
Ripley, don't.

471
00:59:54,048 --> 00:59:55,592
Kill...

472
00:59:56,593 --> 00:59:57,594
...me.

473
01:00:07,562 --> 01:00:09,856
Kill me.

474
01:01:52,041 --> 01:01:54,335
Don't do it, Ripley.

475
01:02:01,384 --> 01:02:03,720
Don't do what?

476
01:02:15,523 --> 01:02:18,276
What's the big deal, man?

477
01:02:18,443 --> 01:02:20,445
Fucking waste of ammo.

478
01:02:20,611 --> 01:02:22,238
Let's go.

479
01:02:24,198 --> 01:02:26,451
It must be a chick thing.

480
01:03:36,187 --> 01:03:39,524
Am I dreaming or is this not
the shit we brought with us?

481
01:03:39,816 --> 01:03:42,402
Yeah. It's the same shit.

482
01:03:43,319 --> 01:03:45,947
It stinks in here, man. Let's keep moving.

483
01:04:17,145 --> 01:04:18,980
Get away from me!

484
01:04:19,188 --> 01:04:20,523
Get away from me!

485
01:04:20,690 --> 01:04:22,775
Get away from me!
Get away from me!

486
01:04:22,942 --> 01:04:24,527
- Drop the rod.
- Get away from me!

487
01:04:24,694 --> 01:04:27,697
- Do it!
- Get away from me.

488
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:31,451
Get away from me.

489
01:04:33,077 --> 01:04:35,288
Who are you people?

490
01:04:35,830 --> 01:04:38,458
- What's happening here?
- Calm down.

491
01:04:38,624 --> 01:04:42,587
What's happening here is we're
getting the fuck off this ghost ship, okay?

492
01:04:43,463 --> 01:04:45,465
Ship? What ship?

493
01:04:46,966 --> 01:04:48,843
Where am I?

494
01:04:49,010 --> 01:04:52,680
I was in cryo, right?
On my way to Xarem, right?

495
01:04:52,847 --> 01:04:55,349
Work crew for the nickel refinery, right?

496
01:04:55,516 --> 01:04:58,811
I wake up...
I know I don't understand.

497
01:05:00,396 --> 01:05:02,440
Oh, God. I--

498
01:05:02,607 --> 01:05:05,485
I saw-- I saw horrible things.

499
01:05:06,319 --> 01:05:09,906
Look, you're coming with us.
It's too dangerous for you here.

500
01:05:20,625 --> 01:05:22,126
Leave him.

501
01:05:22,502 --> 01:05:25,463
Fuck you. We're not leaving him here.

502
01:05:25,755 --> 01:05:29,634
He's got one inside of him. I can smell it.

503
01:05:32,678 --> 01:05:34,472
Inside me?

504
01:05:36,015 --> 01:05:38,518
Inside me? What's inside me?

505
01:05:38,684 --> 01:05:42,021
Hey, I don't want one of those things
birthing anywhere near my ass.

506
01:05:42,188 --> 01:05:46,025
- It's a bad risk.
- What's inside me?

507
01:05:46,275 --> 01:05:49,987
- Look, we can't just leave him here.
- You came here to stop them from spreading.

508
01:05:50,154 --> 01:05:53,032
- What's inside me?
- Gotta be a process. Can't you stop it?

509
01:05:53,199 --> 01:05:56,994
- We've got no time for that.
- We can't do it here. The lab's out of order.

510
01:05:57,161 --> 01:05:58,371
I could do him.

511
01:05:58,538 --> 01:06:01,457
Back of the head. Painless.
It might be the best way.

512
01:06:01,624 --> 01:06:02,708
What's inside me?

513
01:06:02,875 --> 01:06:05,586
- No, there's got to be another way.
- What if we freeze him?

514
01:06:05,753 --> 01:06:07,630
What's in-fucking-side me?!

515
01:06:07,797 --> 01:06:09,632
A parasite!

516
01:06:12,093 --> 01:06:13,302
A foreign element.

517
01:06:19,016 --> 01:06:22,061
There's a monster in your chest.

518
01:06:22,228 --> 01:06:25,314
These guys hijacked your ship...

519
01:06:25,481 --> 01:06:30,319
...and they sold your cryotube
to this human.

520
01:06:30,486 --> 01:06:33,447
And he put an alien inside of you.

521
01:06:33,739 --> 01:06:36,492
It's a really nasty one.

522
01:06:36,659 --> 01:06:40,955
And in a few hours, it's gonna
burst its way through your rib cage...

523
01:06:41,747 --> 01:06:43,583
...and you're gonna die.

524
01:06:49,422 --> 01:06:51,507
Any questions?

525
01:06:57,972 --> 01:06:59,932
Who are you?

526
01:07:01,767 --> 01:07:04,812
I'm the monster's mother.

527
01:07:07,648 --> 01:07:11,277
He comes with us, we freeze him on
the <i>Betty,</i> the doctor can remove it later.

528
01:07:11,569 --> 01:07:14,655
- Fine by me.
- Since when were you in goddamn charge?

529
01:07:14,822 --> 01:07:16,782
Since you were born without balls.

530
01:07:16,991 --> 01:07:19,118
Ease off, people!

531
01:07:27,168 --> 01:07:31,130
All right, you come with us.
You might even live.

532
01:07:31,631 --> 01:07:34,383
Get twitchy on me and you'll be shot.

533
01:07:35,676 --> 01:07:37,386
Let's move out.

534
01:07:48,230 --> 01:07:50,691
It's a mess down there.
Is this the only way?

535
01:07:50,941 --> 01:07:54,820
Vriess. We gotta lose the chair.

536
01:07:56,530 --> 01:07:58,574
I know.

537
01:07:58,741 --> 01:08:02,912
- Kawlang maneuver, right?
- Yeah. Just like old times.

538
01:08:03,079 --> 01:08:04,830
Yeah.

539
01:08:08,918 --> 01:08:11,212
Must be the cooling tanks.

540
01:08:11,379 --> 01:08:13,839
Somebody must have opened the valves.

541
01:08:14,006 --> 01:08:16,842
The nasties couldn't have done this,
could they?

542
01:08:28,562 --> 01:08:31,148
We're at the bottom of the ship.

543
01:08:31,315 --> 01:08:34,527
We have to go through the kitchen.
Maybe 90 feet.

544
01:08:34,694 --> 01:08:37,154
To the freight elevator on the other side.

545
01:08:38,614 --> 01:08:41,450
- I don't like it.
- What's to like?

546
01:08:43,077 --> 01:08:47,248
- This sucks!
- Wren, are you sure about the distance?

547
01:08:47,415 --> 01:08:48,624
Yes.

548
01:08:49,792 --> 01:08:52,753
- You ready to get wet, partner?
- Yeah.

549
01:09:01,262 --> 01:09:04,932
Hey, will your weapons fly underwater?

550
01:09:05,099 --> 01:09:07,518
Yeah, they're disposables.
They can take it.

551
01:09:07,685 --> 01:09:09,061
Disposables?

552
01:09:13,524 --> 01:09:15,901
Hey, I heard about those. Yeah.

553
01:09:18,070 --> 01:09:20,865
- How many rounds?
- Twenty.

554
01:09:21,031 --> 01:09:25,578
Split points give you a good hole,
even if it's smaller caliber.

555
01:09:25,745 --> 01:09:27,747
That's cool.

556
01:09:28,748 --> 01:09:31,917
They're big with hitters
because you throw them away after the job.

557
01:09:32,084 --> 01:09:35,171
Nobody likes to throw away a weapon
they're attached to, you know?

558
01:09:35,337 --> 01:09:36,839
Yeah.

559
01:09:37,006 --> 01:09:40,760
Guess I don't have to tell everyone
to take a deep breath.

560
01:09:45,765 --> 01:09:47,475
Hey, Christie, do me a favor.

561
01:09:47,641 --> 01:09:52,104
When we hit the surface on the other side,
no backstroke, okay?

562
01:13:26,568 --> 01:13:28,362
Jesus Christ!

563
01:13:40,708 --> 01:13:44,878
They set a goddamn trap.
It's a goddamn ambush!

564
01:14:50,736 --> 01:14:52,321
Distephano!

565
01:15:12,633 --> 01:15:15,844
It won't break. Give me your weapon.

566
01:15:16,887 --> 01:15:19,515
You really are way too trusting.

567
01:15:19,681 --> 01:15:20,849
No!

568
01:15:30,818 --> 01:15:32,194
No!

569
01:15:40,869 --> 01:15:44,581
You killed her! You bastard!

570
01:15:48,710 --> 01:15:51,255
I'll get you!

571
01:15:52,673 --> 01:15:55,008
Father, lock the door.

572
01:16:10,357 --> 01:16:12,693
Christie! Climb!

573
01:16:12,860 --> 01:16:14,778
Climb! Come on!

574
01:16:15,195 --> 01:16:17,072
Come on!

575
01:16:17,239 --> 01:16:19,950
It's jammed! Move it!

576
01:16:20,117 --> 01:16:22,494
It's jammed!

577
01:16:55,110 --> 01:16:57,237
Get off my foot, bitch!

578
01:17:10,083 --> 01:17:11,877
Johner!

579
01:17:12,044 --> 01:17:14,129
Get off me! Get off me!

580
01:17:15,797 --> 01:17:17,841
Johner!

581
01:17:21,511 --> 01:17:23,513
Die, motherfucker!

582
01:17:25,641 --> 01:17:27,351
Do it, man!

583
01:17:45,077 --> 01:17:47,496
Real nice party, ain't it?

584
01:18:15,607 --> 01:18:16,817
Christie!

585
01:18:17,693 --> 01:18:19,444
Christie!

586
01:18:20,195 --> 01:18:21,363
Christie!

587
01:18:21,530 --> 01:18:22,948
No!

588
01:18:23,115 --> 01:18:24,783
Christie!

589
01:18:25,867 --> 01:18:27,452
Christie!

590
01:18:27,744 --> 01:18:31,039
What are you doing? Don't do it!

591
01:18:31,373 --> 01:18:32,416
Don't!

592
01:18:32,749 --> 01:18:35,252
We can make it!

593
01:18:35,627 --> 01:18:37,170
No!

594
01:18:41,758 --> 01:18:43,135
Damn.

595
01:19:30,599 --> 01:19:32,434
This way.

596
01:19:35,979 --> 01:19:37,105
Come on!

597
01:19:42,277 --> 01:19:44,112
Baby, am I glad to see you.

598
01:19:44,279 --> 01:19:46,990
I was sure that asshole got you.
Are you hurt?

599
01:19:47,157 --> 01:19:48,909
I'm fine.

600
01:19:49,326 --> 01:19:52,621
- You got body armor on?
- Yeah. Come on.

601
01:19:52,788 --> 01:19:55,624
You took it in the chest. I saw it.

602
01:20:17,354 --> 01:20:19,648
You're a robot?

603
01:20:20,816 --> 01:20:24,027
Son of a bitch! Our little Call
is just full of surprises.

604
01:20:24,194 --> 01:20:28,198
I should've known.
No human being is that humane.

605
01:20:28,365 --> 01:20:30,826
I thought synthetics
were supposed to be logical.

606
01:20:30,992 --> 01:20:33,495
You just a big old psycho, girl.

607
01:20:33,662 --> 01:20:37,082
- You're a robot?
- You're a Second Gen, aren't you?

608
01:20:38,291 --> 01:20:40,419
You're an Auton.

609
01:20:40,669 --> 01:20:44,756
Robots designed by robots, right?

610
01:20:45,549 --> 01:20:46,800
That's right, I remember.

611
01:20:46,967 --> 01:20:49,886
They were supposed to revitalize
the synthetic industry.

612
01:20:50,053 --> 01:20:52,097
Instead they buried it.

613
01:20:52,931 --> 01:20:55,434
They don't like being told what to do.

614
01:20:55,600 --> 01:20:57,727
The government ordered a recall.

615
01:20:57,894 --> 01:20:59,271
Now, I heard...

616
01:20:59,438 --> 01:21:03,442
I had heard that only a few--
Just a few had gotten out in time.

617
01:21:03,608 --> 01:21:06,695
Man, I never thought
that I would see one!

618
01:21:06,945 --> 01:21:10,782
Great. She's a toaster oven.

619
01:21:10,949 --> 01:21:12,951
Can we leave now?

620
01:21:14,995 --> 01:21:18,290
- How long before we land?
- Just under two hours.

621
01:21:18,457 --> 01:21:21,835
Hey, Vriess, you got a socket wrench?
Maybe she just needs an oil change.

622
01:21:22,002 --> 01:21:23,962
I'm sorry. Access denied.

623
01:21:24,129 --> 01:21:28,091
- I can't believe I almost fucked it.
- Yeah, like you never fucked a robot!

624
01:21:28,258 --> 01:21:30,969
You know, if Wren gets in the computer,
he could screw us.

625
01:21:31,136 --> 01:21:34,473
- We gotta find a terminal.
- No, there's no console on this level.

626
01:21:34,639 --> 01:21:37,309
- We'd have to go back.
- Well, we can't go back.

627
01:21:37,476 --> 01:21:39,936
- And I don't know Wren's access codes.
- Help me.

628
01:21:42,439 --> 01:21:43,857
Call.

629
01:21:44,983 --> 01:21:47,027
No, I can't.

630
01:21:47,194 --> 01:21:51,281
Right. You're the new model droid.
You can access the mainframe by remote.

631
01:21:51,448 --> 01:21:55,202
No, I can't. I burned my modem.
We all did.

632
01:21:55,368 --> 01:21:59,164
Call, you can still patch in manually,
you know that.

633
01:21:59,956 --> 01:22:02,918
There's ports in the chapel, up there.

634
01:22:04,503 --> 01:22:06,171
Call.

635
01:22:11,468 --> 01:22:15,180
- You're programmed for that?
- Don't make me do this.

636
01:22:15,347 --> 01:22:18,350
Don't make me make you.

637
01:22:18,517 --> 01:22:20,936
I don't wanna go in there.

638
01:22:21,102 --> 01:22:23,813
It's like my insides are liquid.
It's not real.

639
01:22:24,272 --> 01:22:28,193
Get over it. You can blow this ship
before it reaches Earth...

640
01:22:28,902 --> 01:22:30,195
...and kill them all.

641
01:22:40,705 --> 01:22:43,667
Just give us time to get out first.

642
01:22:46,503 --> 01:22:48,505
- Damn it.
- Anything?

643
01:22:48,672 --> 01:22:50,340
Hold on.

644
01:22:54,719 --> 01:22:58,598
Breach in Sector 7, Sector 3.

645
01:22:58,765 --> 01:23:01,726
Sector 9 unstable.

646
01:23:02,227 --> 01:23:04,688
Engines operating at 41 percent.

647
01:23:04,854 --> 01:23:08,066
Eighty-six minutes until Earth dock.

648
01:23:08,233 --> 01:23:10,277
We burned too much energy.

649
01:23:10,443 --> 01:23:14,406
I can't make critical mass.
I can't blow it.

650
01:23:14,573 --> 01:23:16,074
Then crash it.

651
01:23:29,879 --> 01:23:33,049
I'm okay. I'm okay.

652
01:23:34,092 --> 01:23:35,635
Really.

653
01:23:36,469 --> 01:23:38,179
I feel good.

654
01:23:39,389 --> 01:23:42,100
Ground level recalibrated.

655
01:23:42,267 --> 01:23:47,230
New destination: 7-6-0-4-0-3.
Uninhabited quadrant.

656
01:23:47,856 --> 01:23:52,152
Braking system's offline.
Deceleration increase.

657
01:23:53,361 --> 01:23:57,616
Time until impact
now 43 minutes, 8 seconds.

658
01:23:59,117 --> 01:24:01,953
Try to clear us a path to the <i>Betty.</i>

659
01:24:02,662 --> 01:24:04,205
And start her up.

660
01:24:34,361 --> 01:24:35,779
Please wait.

661
01:24:40,950 --> 01:24:44,329
Emergency override
in console 45V, Level 1.

662
01:24:48,041 --> 01:24:50,251
It's Wren. He's almost at the <i>Betty.</i>

663
01:25:03,723 --> 01:25:07,644
Father, locate the power drain. Report.

664
01:25:09,688 --> 01:25:13,191
Father? Father?

665
01:25:18,279 --> 01:25:21,157
Father's dead, asshole.

666
01:25:24,536 --> 01:25:30,291
Intruder on Level 1.
All aliens, please proceed to Level 1.

667
01:25:30,750 --> 01:25:33,253
You got a mean streak.

668
01:25:37,882 --> 01:25:38,925
Damn it.

669
01:25:39,092 --> 01:25:41,136
- Let me see.
- Don't touch me.

670
01:25:41,302 --> 01:25:42,846
Come on.

671
01:25:43,680 --> 01:25:46,516
You must think this is pretty funny.

672
01:25:47,475 --> 01:25:50,437
I'm finding a lot of things funny lately.

673
01:25:50,603 --> 01:25:53,022
But I don't think they are.

674
01:26:00,613 --> 01:26:03,074
Why do you go on living?

675
01:26:05,160 --> 01:26:07,704
How can you stand being what you are?

676
01:26:09,539 --> 01:26:11,082
Not much choice.

677
01:26:15,211 --> 01:26:17,756
At least there's part of you
that's human.

678
01:26:19,048 --> 01:26:20,633
I'm just...

679
01:26:20,800 --> 01:26:22,093
Look at me.

680
01:26:23,052 --> 01:26:25,263
I'm disgusting.

681
01:26:26,973 --> 01:26:29,392
Why did you come here?

682
01:26:29,559 --> 01:26:31,770
To kill you. Remember?

683
01:26:32,020 --> 01:26:33,897
Before the recall...

684
01:26:34,063 --> 01:26:37,066
...I accessed the mainframe.

685
01:26:37,233 --> 01:26:41,321
Every dirty little covert op
the government ever dreamed up is in there.

686
01:26:41,488 --> 01:26:46,034
And this, you, the aliens,
even the crew from the <i>Betty.</i>

687
01:26:46,201 --> 01:26:49,245
I knew if they succeeded,
it'd be the end of them.

688
01:26:49,412 --> 01:26:51,623
Why do you care what happens to them?

689
01:26:52,540 --> 01:26:54,626
Because I'm programmed to.

690
01:26:55,376 --> 01:26:57,670
You're programmed to be an asshole?

691
01:26:58,880 --> 01:27:01,966
You're the new asshole model
they're putting out?

692
01:27:02,217 --> 01:27:03,468
Come on.

693
01:27:05,512 --> 01:27:08,056
I couldn't watch them do it.

694
01:27:08,223 --> 01:27:11,810
I couldn't let them annihilate themselves.

695
01:27:11,976 --> 01:27:14,312
Do you understand that?

696
01:27:17,315 --> 01:27:19,150
I did once.

697
01:27:19,317 --> 01:27:22,946
I tried to save people.

698
01:27:23,112 --> 01:27:25,573
It didn't work out.

699
01:27:25,740 --> 01:27:28,284
There was this girl.

700
01:27:30,995 --> 01:27:33,706
She had bad dreams.

701
01:27:33,873 --> 01:27:36,668
I tried to help her.

702
01:27:36,876 --> 01:27:38,753
She died.

703
01:27:40,004 --> 01:27:42,841
Now I can't even remember her name.

704
01:27:47,595 --> 01:27:49,639
I guess we're almost there.

705
01:27:50,098 --> 01:27:51,599
Right.

706
01:27:53,434 --> 01:27:59,274
- Do you dream?
- I-- We have neural processors that-- Yes.

707
01:27:59,440 --> 01:28:02,986
When I sleep, I dream about them. It.

708
01:28:03,152 --> 01:28:04,779
Every night.

709
01:28:04,946 --> 01:28:07,240
All around me. In me.

710
01:28:07,407 --> 01:28:10,702
I used to be afraid to dream,
but I'm not anymore.

711
01:28:10,869 --> 01:28:12,495
Why?

712
01:28:13,413 --> 01:28:18,668
Because no matter how bad the dreams
get, when I wake up it's always worse.

713
01:28:22,881 --> 01:28:25,884
- It's not so far now!
- God, I'm so tired!

714
01:28:26,050 --> 01:28:27,510
Sleep when you die, man.

715
01:28:39,063 --> 01:28:41,399
Oh, no. This is bad, right?

716
01:28:42,108 --> 01:28:43,860
I think we're near the nest.

717
01:28:44,027 --> 01:28:47,113
- Well, then, we'll go another way.
- We don't have time.

718
01:28:47,280 --> 01:28:49,282
- We got nearly 90 minutes.
- Not anymore.

719
01:28:49,699 --> 01:28:51,242
What are you saying?

720
01:28:51,409 --> 01:28:54,329
- What did you do, robot?
- Let's go. Come on.

721
01:28:54,495 --> 01:28:58,875
Hey! You wanna die here with your
little brothers and sisters, that's cool.

722
01:28:59,042 --> 01:29:01,210
But I plan to live past today.

723
01:29:01,377 --> 01:29:04,339
If this little hunk of plastic
is pulling any shit...

724
01:29:04,505 --> 01:29:06,132
...I'm gonna kill her!

725
01:29:07,300 --> 01:29:08,593
Kill you!

726
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:12,430
Does that compute?
Or do I have to draw you a schematic?

727
01:29:13,264 --> 01:29:15,058
Hey!

728
01:29:17,560 --> 01:29:19,687
You want another souvenir?

729
01:29:26,986 --> 01:29:29,781
- How far are the docks?
- A hundred yards.

730
01:29:41,000 --> 01:29:42,710
Ripley?

731
01:29:44,128 --> 01:29:46,214
Ripley?

732
01:29:47,048 --> 01:29:49,133
Come on.

733
01:29:49,300 --> 01:29:51,636
Ripley, we have to go.

734
01:29:53,137 --> 01:29:57,016
I hear them. I hear them.
They're so close.

735
01:29:58,059 --> 01:30:00,186
- Ripley.
- It's the queen.

736
01:30:00,978 --> 01:30:03,439
She's in pain.

737
01:30:06,442 --> 01:30:08,403
Ripley!

738
01:30:08,861 --> 01:30:10,988
Ripley!

739
01:30:11,155 --> 01:30:12,907
Wait!

740
01:30:35,179 --> 01:30:36,556
Oh, my God.

741
01:30:49,193 --> 01:30:54,282
We gotta be moving. The best thing
we can do is pray for a quick death.

742
01:30:54,949 --> 01:30:57,785
Come on. Come on.

743
01:30:57,952 --> 01:31:02,206
- It's not right.
- I've been saying that all day.

744
01:31:59,597 --> 01:32:00,848
It's up to you now, Call.

745
01:32:01,015 --> 01:32:04,811
I need you to patch into the ship again,
and open the hatch.

746
01:32:15,446 --> 01:32:18,574
Johner, we should put Purvis
in the freezer now.

747
01:32:18,741 --> 01:32:20,785
All right, little buddy.

748
01:32:21,744 --> 01:32:23,538
Nap time.

749
01:32:30,920 --> 01:32:35,299
Nobody moves, or I put a cap
right where this little droid's brain is.

750
01:32:36,259 --> 01:32:40,638
- Distephano, take the weapons.
- Begging your pardon, sir, but fuck you!

751
01:32:40,805 --> 01:32:43,099
Oh, fine. Then I kill her...

752
01:32:43,266 --> 01:32:45,810
...and you kill me, and we all die...

753
01:32:45,977 --> 01:32:47,562
...and nobody goes home!

754
01:32:47,812 --> 01:32:50,773
Now drop the weapon.

755
01:32:54,610 --> 01:32:58,739
Then this little synthetic bitch
is gonna plug into the <i>Auriga...</i>

756
01:32:58,906 --> 01:33:01,659
...and she is gonna take us
right back to home base...

757
01:33:01,826 --> 01:33:04,495
...according to the standard
emergency procedures.

758
01:33:04,662 --> 01:33:06,956
- No, she's not.
- Are you crazy?

759
01:33:07,123 --> 01:33:09,375
You still wanna bring those things
back to Earth?

760
01:33:09,542 --> 01:33:13,462
- Haven't you been paying attention today?
- The intellectual speaks.

761
01:33:14,630 --> 01:33:18,593
- Listen, if you don't--
- Don't you ever shut up?

762
01:33:30,646 --> 01:33:32,273
Why does nobody listen to me?

763
01:34:16,317 --> 01:34:20,988
I told you, at first everything was normal.
The queen laid her eggs.

764
01:34:21,155 --> 01:34:25,743
But then she started to change.
She added a second cycle, so...

765
01:34:28,704 --> 01:34:30,414
So...

766
01:34:34,752 --> 01:34:38,047
...this time there is no host.

767
01:34:38,214 --> 01:34:40,591
There are no eggs.

768
01:34:40,758 --> 01:34:44,428
There is only her womb...

769
01:34:44,595 --> 01:34:47,306
...and the creature inside.

770
01:34:47,473 --> 01:34:53,938
That is Ripley's gift to her,
a human reproductive system.

771
01:34:54,105 --> 01:34:57,400
She is giving birth for you, Ripley.

772
01:34:57,566 --> 01:35:01,904
And now she is perfect!

773
01:36:27,031 --> 01:36:30,367
You are...

774
01:36:30,785 --> 01:36:36,832
...a beautiful, beautiful butterfly.

775
01:37:04,819 --> 01:37:05,903
No!

776
01:37:10,908 --> 01:37:12,368
No. No.

777
01:38:06,922 --> 01:38:08,632
Look.

778
01:38:08,799 --> 01:38:13,512
Look, beautiful, beautiful little baby.

779
01:38:14,597 --> 01:38:16,807
Look, it thinks you're its mother.

780
01:38:22,188 --> 01:38:23,355
Come on.

781
01:38:24,648 --> 01:38:26,609
Come on.

782
01:38:34,783 --> 01:38:36,285
Come on.

783
01:38:53,844 --> 01:38:58,307
Civilian vessel online.
Emergency departure authorized.

784
01:39:02,228 --> 01:39:06,690
All right, she's hot. I'll open the <i>Auriga</i>'s
air locks. Pull the holding clamps.

785
01:39:07,024 --> 01:39:12,363
Right, I just need to find
the vertical thrust lock.

786
01:39:17,701 --> 01:39:20,496
- Are you sure you guys can fly this thing?
- Yes.

787
01:39:34,760 --> 01:39:38,222
- Launch status is go.
- No!

788
01:39:40,307 --> 01:39:41,934
Ripley.

789
01:40:10,587 --> 01:40:12,256
- Hey.
- I thought you were dead.

790
01:40:12,423 --> 01:40:14,341
Yeah, I get that a lot.

791
01:40:14,925 --> 01:40:21,265
- Why are we still here?
- I'm just finding the manual override.

792
01:40:21,932 --> 01:40:23,392
- For chrissake.
- Hey, Ripley.

793
01:40:23,559 --> 01:40:25,436
Good memory. Excuse me.

794
01:40:25,602 --> 01:40:27,271
- Ripley's back, man.
- Is that it?

795
01:40:27,438 --> 01:40:28,939
Nope.

796
01:40:29,481 --> 01:40:31,608
You can't fly one of these things too,
can you?

797
01:40:31,775 --> 01:40:35,029
Are you kidding?
This piece of shit is even older than I am.

798
01:40:35,195 --> 01:40:38,574
Goddamn it! We still got breach.
The hatch.

799
01:40:38,741 --> 01:40:41,702
- I closed it.
- I've fixed the hatch a hundred times, man.

800
01:40:41,869 --> 01:40:44,496
I'll get it. I'll get it.

801
01:41:06,310 --> 01:41:12,900
Approaching Earth's atmosphere.
Window of departure now 46 seconds.

802
01:41:14,318 --> 01:41:17,237
Call? We have to go.

803
01:41:18,614 --> 01:41:20,324
Call.

804
01:41:22,910 --> 01:41:24,703
We've gotta get out of here.

805
01:41:29,375 --> 01:41:33,796
Window of departure now 20 seconds.

806
01:41:36,840 --> 01:41:40,344
Grab on to something, Call.
We're out of here.

807
01:41:56,026 --> 01:41:57,528
Come on, baby.

808
01:42:10,707 --> 01:42:13,252
This thing is gonna fall apart.

809
01:42:13,419 --> 01:42:16,088
Pressure's unstable!

810
01:42:20,592 --> 01:42:23,846
Go help Call turn on the auxiliary pump.

811
01:42:51,248 --> 01:42:52,291
Distephano?

812
01:43:13,896 --> 01:43:15,981
Come on. Step on it.

813
01:43:16,148 --> 01:43:19,276
Hey! I'm not the mechanic here, Ironside.

814
01:43:19,443 --> 01:43:22,070
I mostly just hurt people.

815
01:43:22,237 --> 01:43:23,322
Shit.

816
01:43:23,489 --> 01:43:25,782
Call!

817
01:43:25,949 --> 01:43:28,785
Call, get back up here.

818
01:43:29,745 --> 01:43:32,414
Call! Call!

819
01:43:33,665 --> 01:43:37,085
Ripley. Hey, Ripley!

820
01:43:41,965 --> 01:43:46,053
Johner, where are you, you son of a bitch?
Get on it, bastard.

821
01:43:46,220 --> 01:43:49,765
- What am I supposed to do?
- Grab the sticks.

822
01:44:04,279 --> 01:44:06,156
Put her down.

823
01:45:43,420 --> 01:45:45,589
Ripley!

824
01:46:12,532 --> 01:46:14,451
I'm sorry.

825
01:46:44,523 --> 01:46:48,860
USM <i>Auriga</i> will impact in five seconds.
Four.

826
01:46:49,820 --> 01:46:51,071
Three.

827
01:46:51,238 --> 01:46:53,573
Two. One.

828
01:46:53,740 --> 01:46:54,783
Thank you.

829
01:47:19,850 --> 01:47:21,768
- What's burning?
- Us!

830
01:47:24,229 --> 01:47:26,648
Shit! You're right.

831
01:48:47,020 --> 01:48:49,564
So this is Earth, huh?

832
01:48:51,399 --> 01:48:53,443
This is Earth.

833
01:48:56,822 --> 01:48:59,449
It's my first time here.

834
01:49:03,286 --> 01:49:07,791
I suppose the military'll be
sniffing around here pretty soon.

835
01:49:07,958 --> 01:49:10,544
Bet you're not too anxious to see them.

836
01:49:10,710 --> 01:49:12,587
Not really.

837
01:49:13,797 --> 01:49:17,634
You know, a person could get pretty lost
around here if they wanted to.

838
01:49:19,845 --> 01:49:21,972
What do you think?

839
01:49:22,138 --> 01:49:24,891
What should we do?

840
01:49:25,058 --> 01:49:27,060
I don't know.

841
01:49:28,436 --> 01:49:31,439
I'm a stranger here myself.

842
01:56:04,540 --> 01:56:06,542
[ENGLISH - US]

